#: ../../source/docs/common-autopilots.rst:220
#: ../../source/docs/common-autopilots.rst:224
#: 3cad38a96a69473595fd77d982a1a396 52694a64aa4e4748a473db78ff365343
#: 5d40673e19854f67b4f400a8d98ab2be cb75b2f9018248ac8842d65517ae03a4
#: f4c43a74d14a4c9996544b7c54876b20
msgid ""
"These autopilots use an underlying Linux OS. Linux boards usually have more "
"CPU power and memory many of the other boards listed on this page, but do "
"not support DShot, Bi-Directional DShot, BLHeli ESC passthrough, many of the"
" ArduPilot GPIO based features, and easy upload from the ground stations. "
"They do allow experimentation and development of advanced control and "
"navigation algorithms (see also :ref:`common-companion-computers`)."
msgstr ""
"这些飞控使用底层 Linux 操作系统。Linux 板通常比本页列出的其他飞控板拥有更强的 CPU 算力和更大的内存，但不支持 DShot、双向 "
"DShot、BLHeli ESC 直通、许多 ArduPilot GPIO "
"相关功能以及从地面站直接上传固件。它们允许对高级控制和导航算法进行实验和开发（另见 :ref:`common-companion-"
"computers`）。"

